NOTICE — UML engine components shipped in this application
==========================================================

This application ships the UML (User Mode Linux) engine family inside the
main APK: the pinned fast-profile kernel pair (lib/arm64-v8a/libuml_kernel.so
and lib/arm64-v8a/libuml_stub.so), the umnet/passt network helper pair
(lib/arm64-v8a/libuml_net.so and lib/arm64-v8a/libuml_passt.so) and the
Alpine minirootfs baseline tar (alpine-minirootfs-3.22.2-aarch64.tar.gz,
packaged as a java resource at the APK root). The complete license/source
record for the QEMU engine is in NOTICE.QEMU, QEMU-GPL-SOURCES.md and
QEMU-BUILD-INPUTS packaged alongside this notice; this file covers only the
UML lane's own components. It is the formalized successor of the drafting
record kept during the UML productization research (the draft's registry of
what had to be true before the assets could ship); the assets this notice
describes are real, packaged bytes, verified at build time and at the
artifact level by the release gates.

UML kernel
----------
The kernel is Linux modified for User Mode Linux on ARM64. Modified-version
distribution follows the GPL-2.0 obligations: the modified source is public,
the binary in this APK is pinned, and the release flow keeps the binary and
its corresponding source in a one-to-one relationship (see "Corresponding
source" below).

  - Fork: Raymer8639/linux-um-arm64, public tag `um-arm64-v0.3.0`
    (Linux 7.2.0-rc4, commit 169b17ff3f66d507cb137b770ceb1fd9f4547a32).
  - Source tarball sha256:
    08578a494412125dfc6b8f203e984b68d20e313173319d6a6c115e2875e0116c
  - Product pins (ARM64 UP build, registry order):
      linux-fast            21e1c3f97269a831fa8bab5fd3ff0e8a0e9edc59554d17cce34913924f584389
      linux-fast-noinitrd   a5efce2b9197071a2db89735e247fa3cf548644b7d036ea99bf688b14eff17fb
      stub_exe              87666f9167de09d0bf84b414618c39d9f460417a641f212f5f0f28c498a09a12
      initramfs.cpio.gz     7523c9a20b956a3104d04540559422a7b566ef630a592c9d4ca8fdb2e5bd8381
    The single pin source is the PIN_MANIFEST constant in
    app/src/main/java/io/github/nyzeep/orchestella/UmlKernelAssets.java — the
    build-time accounting, the runtime verification and the release gates all
    read that one registry. OPEN: the device-window build of `linux-fast` (the
    kernel variant with the initramfs embedded) did not reproduce the pinned
    digest across build paths (observed 572c3433…, same size, difference
    isolated to the embedded initramfs segment); the shipped pin is the
    reproducible container-build artifact (21e1c3f9…), and the cross-path
    variance is recorded here rather than papered over. An artifact that does
    not match the shipped pin fails closed at runtime — the pin governs.
  - Configuration delivery: research/uml-fastboot/defconfig-fast plus
    research/uml-fastboot/defconfig-fast.fragment, derived from the pinned
    linux-bionic.config via olddefconfig; the final kernel.config and
    kernel-noinitrd.config digests are recorded in
    research/uml-fastboot/manifest.md (§3). These out-of-tree control scripts
    are part of the preferred form for modification (GPLv2 §2) and ship in the
    same public repository.
  - Build environment: research/uml-fastboot/build-fast.sh is the build
    entrypoint; Android NDK r29 (official zip sha256 4abbbcdc…08ecf); build
    container Ubuntu 24.04 with GCC 13.3.0; KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP and
    SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH are fixed. Two clean rebuilds on the same container
    layout are byte-identical (the cross-path variance above is a separate,
    recorded phenomenon). The 16 KB page-size stub relink recipe is
    research/uml-kernel-build/build-stub-16k.sh; the 16 KB ELF checks are
    recorded in the build research, not here.

stub_exe
--------
libuml_stub.so is this project's own work (a 16 KB-relinked helper, byte-
identical to the release stub recipe). It is distributed under this
project's root LICENSE (GPL-3.0-or-later). OPEN: the final licensing-attribution
ruling for this artifact is reserved to the project's licensing decision
record; this notice states the current practice without claiming a closed
verdict.

initramfs content
-----------------
The initramfs embedded in / shipped next to the kernel carries
busybox-static 1.37.0-r20 (Alpine 3.22, GPL-2.0; aarch64 apk
ee469aee…34da2, binary a6bb1e6e…004ff; x86_64 apk 488ad6ef…c74b) and this
project's own scripts research/uml-fastboot/initramfs/init and
research/uml-fastboot/initramfs/um-command.sh. The embedded decompressor is
gzip only.

rootfs baseline (Alpine minirootfs)
-----------------------------------
The guest rootfs baseline is the official Alpine minirootfs 3.22.2 for
aarch64: alpine-minirootfs-3.22.2-aarch64.tar.gz, sha256
6bf491907b705caa5fc65773fbbc1d0954530b6c455d4446f670a4c1fdcea489
(3,981,043 bytes, locked against the release CDN and the distro's own
.sha256 sidecar). It travels one asset, two transport lines: embedded in
this APK (consumed by the provisioner first) and downloadable from
https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.22/releases/aarch64/ as the repair
channel; both lines verify the same fixed pin at runtime (constant-time
digest compare, fail-closed) — no GPG verification runs on device. The
upstream package license inventory rides the tar's apk database. The tree
the provisioner extracts is a project-modified version of the minirootfs
(it injects /um-command.sh, the external-root launcher described below),
which triggers the corresponding-source obligation for the injected files;
the launcher is this project's own script and its source is public in the
same repository.

um-command.sh launcher
----------------------
The provisioner injects a project-owned launcher script
(research/uml-fastboot/initramfs/um-command.sh is its source of record)
into the extracted rootfs. It is this project's work, distributed under
this project's root LICENSE (GPL-3.0-or-later), and is a launch-chain
preparation, not a capability promise.

umnet/passt network helpers
---------------------------
libuml_net.so (the umnet supervisor, built from the passt-android fork's
umnet harness with this project's loopback-only inbound forward patch) and
libuml_passt.so (passt, built from the passt-android fork at its v0.2.0
pin) are statically linked bionic executables carrying a .so name for the
jniLibs packaging convention. passt is GPL-2.0-or-later (see its upstream
source); the umnet harness and the forwarding patch are distributed with
the same public repository as the rest of the corresponding source. The
inbound forward binds loopback only (127.0.0.1:3632) and serves the guest's
distccd compile route; there is no UDP inbound and no LAN exposure.

Corresponding source and written offer
--------------------------------------
The corresponding source for every GPL component above is public: the
modified UML kernel at the fixed tag, the build and configuration scripts
under research/uml-fastboot/, and the project-owned scripts named here. The
written-offer text for the guest-runtime assets is guest-assets/SOURCE-OFFER.txt
(the template this project distributes with the QEMU lane); the UML
components ride the same written-offer channel. OPEN: a UML-specific
BUILD-INPUTS identifier and the ADR-style one-to-one release source package
are process items that ride the release flow; the pin registry in this
repository is the binding identity record in the meantime.

Upgrade discipline
------------------
A UML kernel upgrade is one atomic change: a new fixed public tag, a new
matching source record, and new PIN_MANIFEST values, updated in the same
change as the binary. Shipped bytes and this notice must never disagree.
